  "term": "discharge rate",
  "definition": "Discharge rate is the rate at which a neuron fires during stimulation. In this context, it refers to the strength of the neuron’s overall response as measured by its mean firing rate, which can vary separately from oscillatory modulation tied to the stimulus frequency.",
